    "reviewed_associations": [
      "The seven formal Syphon pages consistently document one melee variant, the exact full double-bespoke trait ID, and two bindings for Powersword Munitorum Mk X and Mk II. The entry, compatibility table, catalog, melee reverse index, weapon reverse page, and map retain the same actual ID, names, classification, icon and shared four-tier values.",
      "The canonical config and extension-draft configuration are structurally equal. Both retain the exact inventory trait ID, actual buff template/source path, 1-variant/2-binding counts, per-weapon restriction, icon ID/path/attachment separation, and unverified/disabled FASTER state. The frozen agent config/draft/evidence hashes remain unchanged.",
      "The RAW name/description keys and hashes agree with the bilingual fixed-resource receipt. Localization comparison preserves the exact English and Traditional Chinese templates and reconstructs all four formatter outputs (+10%, +12%, +14%, +16%) from the own-tier values; it labels reconstruction as static rather than captured gameplay.",
      "The image 240 receipt matches the formal icon path and public attachment; its recorded PNG SHA-256, 128×128 dimensions, public-byte verification and visual review are consistent."
    ],
    "reviewed_deltas": [
      "The exact variant ID intentionally contains repeated bespoke and matches its actual wrapper. Own tiers use toughness_fixed_percentage=.10/.12/.14/.16; wrapper .15 is only a fallback replaced by tier data, not an added bonus.",
      "The current eligible melee Attack.on_hit payload is tested with target_number>=3. This is the current sweep target ordinal, not an accumulation of three earlier eligible on_hit events; the first two ordinals need not each dispatch on_hit. ActionSweep increments its local ordinal before resolution, while its persistent enemy count has a narrower alive-character branch. The documents do not equate the ordinal with three positive-damage enemies and preserve candidate/Attack gates without globalizing breakable behavior.",
      "The wrapper latches special_active at on_sweep_start and requires the held slot and exact item. When the current qualifying target-number event passes, it clears can_activate before calling recover_percentage_toughness. Thus a full toughness bar or state-gated recovery rejection does not restore the one-per-sweep attempt; the next sweep re-reads eligibility.",
      "Recovery requests current max toughness × tier fraction and caps actual restore at missing toughness. ignore_stat_buffs=true bypasses only the replenish stat multiplier. The docs retain downed/dead/prohibited-state checks and the force_assist exception; examples compute 16 requested/16 restored from 100 max and 60 current, and 16 requested/4 restored from 96 current.",
      "Actual ordinary light/heavy/sprint and push-follow paths use sweep; ordinary push is push-kind. M1/M2 special-toggle actions map to the toggle executors and WeaponSpecialCharging; the cited 66–81 handler changes charge_template and is not a qualifying hit action. SOURCE_INDEX includes exact M1/M2 action ranges, both executor ranges, and the special-class range.",
      "The map summary, reverse pages and formal player text use the same ordinal/attempt wording and 10/12/14/16% requested-recovery values. The special toggle itself is not documented as an attack or recovery trigger."
    ],
